------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The scoring method shipped with the tool
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Open TARA method 1.0" (methods/open-tara-1.0.json) was built from sources that
are free to reuse. The file itself names the source and terms of each part:

- Attack feasibility (the five factors, their points and the bands):
  Common Methodology for Information Technology Security Evaluation,
  CEM:2022, November 2022, Annex B.6, Tables B.2 and B.3. Common Criteria
  portal, commoncriteriaportal.org. The descriptions are written anew.

- Risk matrix (the sixteen values):
  A. Lautenbach, M. Almgren, T. Olovsson: "Proposing HEAVENS 2.0, an automotive
  risk assessment model". ACM Computer Science in Cars Symposium (CSCS '21),
  2021, Table 8. doi:10.1145/3488904.3493378. The values are used and cited;
  no text of the paper is used.

- Structure (impact in four categories at four levels, attack feasibility at
  four levels, risk values 1 to 5): follows the requirements of
  ISO/SAE 21434:2021, clause 15. Only the structure is taken. No text of the
  standard is reproduced in this project, and none must be added to it.

- Impact criteria, descriptions of factors, threat categories and treatments:
  written for this method.

